---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SectionHero from "../../components/SectionHero.astro";
import cases from "../../../public/agentic-le/cases.json";
import run from "../../../public/agentic-le/replay/live-exemplar.json";
const modelResponses = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "request").length;
const artifacts = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "artifact").length;
---
<Base title="Agentic LE · Capability Matters" active="problems-to-prototypes"
 description="From a seed idea to a runnable candidate product, with public agent discussion, scenario challenges, evidence and versioned artifacts.">
 <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
 <SectionHero eyebrow="Problems → Prototypes → Products" title="A product, with its work shown."
 claim="A learning engineer orchestrates specialist roles through a revisitable project lifecycle. The runnable candidate, the discussion that shaped it, and its evidence limits travel together."
 question="What changed the design—and what would justify putting it into real use?" />
 <section class="container lab">
  <p><a href="/agentic-le/paper/"><strong>Read the working paper: Learning Engineering Teams at Work</strong></a></p>
  <div class="actions"><a href="/agentic-le/product/">Try the generated product</a><a href="/agentic-le/replay/">Replay the project</a><a href="/agentic-le/product/product.zip" download>Download product bundle</a></div>
  <article id="cases"><h2>Explore diverse live-agent cases</h2><p>Actual model agents worked on fictional problems in workforce feedback, school science and public-library digital access. Each case retains its discussion, hypothetical challenges, revisions and generated candidate. Human pilot approval and field evidence remain pending.</p><div class="grid">{cases.cases.map(c => <div><h3>{c.title}</h3><p>{c.counts.request} recorded model calls · {c.counts.artifact} artifact versions · {c.counts.scenario} hypothetical challenges</p><p><a href={`/agentic-le/replay/?case=${c.id}`}>Replay this case</a> · <a href={c.product}>Try its candidate</a> · <a href={`${c.product}product.zip`} download>Download its record and product</a></p></div>)}</div><p><a href="/agentic-le/cases.json">Inspect case inventory and journal hashes</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/CASES.md">Expansion checklist</a></p></article>
  <div class="grid">
   <article><h2>The product</h2><p><strong>{run.seed.title}</strong> helps a new team lead rehearse a fictional feedback decision, consider another explanation, revise an approach and recover from an interruption. Its reflection is descriptive; it does not assess employees.</p><p>The handoff contains executable HTML, requirements, versioned artifacts, the project journal and a source-linked manifest. It is a candidate product requiring affected-person review and field validation.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/product/manifest.json">Inspect the product handoff</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/product/requirements.md">Read the requirements</a></p></article>
   <article><h2>The project record</h2><p>The saved fictional workforce project contains {modelResponses} real model responses, including a rejected correction, and {artifacts} artifact versions. Scenarios changed interruption privacy and reviewer-conflict requirements. An actual missing-code finding reopened Build.</p><p>The replay preserves original drafts, dissent, prompts, provider metadata, failed validation and the corrected candidate. Recorded browser checks support only the behavior exercised in that environment.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/replay/live-exemplar.json">Inspect the source journal</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/replay/">Follow the revisions</a></p></article>
  </div>
  <article><h2>Reusable roles and proficiency targets</h2><p>Roles inherit a common contribution contract, then specialize by discipline and relevant domain. They reference the five LENS competency domains. Requested proficiency describes the contribution expected in a simulation; demonstrated proficiency requires separately reviewed task evidence.</p><p>The existing exemplar used earlier fixed prompts. Its history is preserved without retrospectively assigning these new targets. Future runs pin the resolved role profiles and their versions in the journal.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/roles/">Explore roles, inheritance and evidence requirements</a></p></article>
  <article><h2>From candidate to operational product</h2><p>Understand → Model → Design → Build → Instrument → Deploy → Evaluate → Refine is a revisitable cycle. Build produces the executable candidate; refinement can return to any invalidated requirement. The learning engineer integrates the work and keeps human and system requirements visible.</p><p>Real use needs accountable ownership, affected-person review, appropriate data handling, accessible operation, a meaningful comparison and stopping rules. Learning, workplace transfer and flourishing remain claims to investigate. Inadequate conditions can justify changing the product, changing the work system, or stopping.</p><p>The hosted site serves saved products and replay. New model runs use the local runner in this repository; hosted model access and a shared job queue remain future work.</p></article>
  <p class="source"><a href="/problems-to-prototypes/">Return to project seeds</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/tools/lifecycle">Runner source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/docs/lifecycle">Specification and operating documentation</a></p>
 </section>
</Base>
<style>#cases{scroll-margin-top:5rem}.lab{padding-top:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.4rem}article{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.4rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem;background:var(--bg)}h2{font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:0}.actions{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1.5rem}.actions a{background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:.7rem 1rem;border-radius:4px;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem;text-decoration:none}.source{font-size:.9rem}@media(max-width:700px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
